{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And Pharaoh said concerning the children of Israel.</b> Like אמרי לי (Genesis 20:13)." "<b>נבוכים [bewildered].</b> With shureq in place of cholam, like לא תעבורי מזה (Ruth 2:8), for it is of the nifal pattern, like נכונים (below 19:11) and והנה נבוכו (Joel 1:18), also והעיר שושן נבוכה (Esther 3:15), like והממלכה נכונה (1 Kings 2:46). The meaning is like a person who finds no counsel and does not know what to do. And the nun of נִבְכֵּי ים (Job 38:16) is a root letter, and its meaning is 'depths of the sea,' and it has no meaning in this place." "<b>The wilderness has shut upon them.</b> That the ways of the wilderness were closed upon them, and they did not know where to go and where to depart, like fugitives."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:34:20.461555705Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}